"response": [
{
"value": "This error occurs because PowerShell script blocks (`$ProcessLine`) cannot be invoked from a background thread (like those used by `Process.OutputDataReceived` and `Process.ErrorDataReceived`). PowerShell runspaces are not available in those threads, so you get the \"no Runspace available\" exception.\n\n**How to fix:** \nInstead of using asynchronous event handlers with script blocks, read the process output synchronously after the process exits. Here’s how you can refactor your code:\n\n````powershell\n",
"supportThemeIcons": false,
"supportHtml": false,
"baseUri": {
"$mid": 1,
"path": "/C:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.IAC.Ansible.Powershell/",
"scheme": "file"
}
},
{
"kind": "codeblockUri",
"uri": {
"$mid": 1,
"fsPath": "c:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.IAC.Ansible.Powershell\\public\\Get-ChocolateyPackagesNeedingUpdate.ps1",
"_sep": 1,
"external": "file:///c%3A/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.IAC.Ansible.Powershell/public/Get-ChocolateyPackagesNeedingUpdate.ps1",
"path": "/C:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.IAC.Ansible.Powershell/public/Get-ChocolateyPackagesNeedingUpdate.ps1",
"scheme": "file"
}
},
{
"value": "...existing code...\n PROCESS {\n\n # Start process\n $process.Start() | Out-Null\n\n # Read output synchronously\n $stdOut = $process.StandardOutput.ReadToEnd()\n $stdErr = $process.StandardError.ReadToEnd()\n\n # Wait for exit\n $process.WaitForExit()\n $exitCode = $process.ExitCode\n\n # Process stdout lines\n $lines = $stdOut -split \"`r?`n\"\n $script:lineNumber = 0\n foreach ($line in $lines) {\n if ($script:lineNumber -lt $discardPreambleLines) {\n $script:lineNumber++\n continue\n }\n if ($line -match $regexPattern) {\n Write-Output $line\n }\n else {\n Write-PSFMessage -Level Error -Message \"$line did not match the pattern $regexPattern. Line number $script:lineNumber was $line\"\n }\n $script:lineNumber++\n }\n\n # Process stderr lines\n if ($stdErr) {\n $errLines = $stdErr -split \"`r?`n\"\n foreach ($errLine in $errLines) {\n if ($errLine) {\n Write-PSFMessage -Level Warning -Message \"Choco warning: $errLine\" -Tag 'Trace', 'Get-ChocolateyPackagesNeedingUpdate'\n }\n }\n }\n\n return $exitCode\n }\n...existing code...\n````\n\n**Summary:** \n- Remove the asynchronous event handlers.\n- Read output synchronously after process exit.\n- Process each line in PowerShell’s main runspace.\n\nThis will resolve the runspace error and allow your script block logic to work.",
"supportThemeIcons": false,
"supportHtml": false,
