"response": [
{
"value": "To process each line from stdout as it is produced, you must use PowerShell jobs or runspaces, because .NET event handlers for `OutputDataReceived` run on background threads and cannot invoke PowerShell script blocks directly (as you saw with the runspace error).\n\n**Solution:** \nUse a `[System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentQueue[string]]` to collect lines in the event handler, then process them in the main thread after the process exits.\n\nHere’s how you can do it:\n\n`powershell\n",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/C:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.IAC.Ansible.Powershell/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "codeblockUri",
          "uri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "fsPath": "c:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.IAC.Ansible.Powershell\\public\\Get-ChocolateyPackagesNeedingUpdate.ps1",
            "_sep": 1,
            "external": "file:///c%3A/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.IAC.Ansible.Powershell/public/Get-ChocolateyPackagesNeedingUpdate.ps1",
            "path": "/C:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.IAC.Ansible.Powershell/public/Get-ChocolateyPackagesNeedingUpdate.ps1",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        },
        {
          "value": "...existing code...\n  BEGIN {\n    ...existing code...\n    $outputQueue = [System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentQueue[string]]::new()\n    $errorQueue = [System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentQueue[string]]::new()\n\n    $process.add_OutputDataReceived({\n      param($sender, $args)\n      if ($args.Data) {\n        $outputQueue.Enqueue($args.Data)\n      }\n    })\n\n    $process.add_ErrorDataReceived({\n      param($sender, $args)\n      if ($args.Data) {\n        $errorQueue.Enqueue($args.Data)\n      }\n    })\n    ...existing code...\n  }\n\n  PROCESS {\n    $process.Start() | Out-Null\n    $process.BeginOutputReadLine()\n    $process.BeginErrorReadLine()\n    $process.WaitForExit()\n    $exitCode = $process.ExitCode\n\n    $script:lineNumber = 0\n    while ($outputQueue.TryDequeue([ref]$line)) {\n      if ($script:lineNumber -lt $discardPreambleLines) {\n        $script:lineNumber++\n        continue\n      }\n      if ($line -match $regexPattern) {\n        Write-Output $line\n      }\n      else {\n        Write-PSFMessage -Level Error -Message \"$line did not match the pattern $regexPattern. Line number $script:lineNumber was $line\"\n      }\n      $script:lineNumber++\n    }\n\n    while ($errorQueue.TryDequeue([ref]$errLine)) {\n      Write-PSFMessage -Level Warning -Message \"Choco warning: $errLine\" -Tag 'Trace', 'Get-ChocolateyPackagesNeedingUpdate'\n    }\n\n    return $exitCode\n  }\n...existing code...\n`\n\n**Summary:** \n- Use concurrent queues to collect output/error lines in the event handler.\n- After process exits, dequeue and process each line in the main thread/runspace.\n- This lets you handle lines as they arrive, without runspace errors.",
