"response": [
{
"value": "You cannot invoke PowerShell script blocks directly from .NET event handlers because they run on background threads without a PowerShell runspace, which causes the error you saw. \n**However, you can queue the lines in the event handler and use a timer or loop in your main runspace to process them as they arrive, without waiting for process exit.**\n\nHere’s how you can do it:\n\n`powershell\n",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/C:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.IAC.Ansible.Powershell/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "codeblockUri",
          "uri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "fsPath": "c:\\Dropbox\\whertzing\\GitHub\\ATAP.Utilities\\src\\ATAP.Utilities.IAC.Ansible.Powershell\\public\\Get-ChocolateyPackagesNeedingUpdate.ps1",
            "_sep": 1,
            "external": "file:///c%3A/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.IAC.Ansible.Powershell/public/Get-ChocolateyPackagesNeedingUpdate.ps1",
            "path": "/C:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.IAC.Ansible.Powershell/public/Get-ChocolateyPackagesNeedingUpdate.ps1",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        },
        {
          "value": "...existing code...\n  BEGIN {\n    ...existing code...\n    $outputQueue = [System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentQueue[string]]::new()\n    $errorQueue = [System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentQueue[string]]::new()\n\n    $process.add_OutputDataReceived({\n      param($sender, $args)\n      if ($args.Data) {\n        $outputQueue.Enqueue($args.Data)\n      }\n    })\n\n    $process.add_ErrorDataReceived({\n      param($sender, $args)\n      if ($args.Data) {\n        $errorQueue.Enqueue($args.Data)\n      }\n    })\n    ...existing code...\n  }\n\n  PROCESS {\n    $process.Start() | Out-Null\n    $process.BeginOutputReadLine()\n    $process.BeginErrorReadLine()\n\n    # Process lines as they arrive, without waiting for process exit\n    while (-not $process.HasExited) {\n      while ($outputQueue.TryDequeue([ref]$line)) {\n        & $ProcessLine $line\n      }\n      while ($errorQueue.TryDequeue([ref]$errLine)) {\n        Write-PSFMessage -Level Warning -Message \"Choco warning: $errLine\" -Tag 'Trace', 'Get-ChocolateyPackagesNeedingUpdate'\n      }\n      Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 100\n    }\n\n    # Process any remaining lines after exit\n    while ($outputQueue.TryDequeue([ref]$line)) {\n      & $ProcessLine $line\n    }\n    while ($errorQueue.TryDequeue([ref]$errLine)) {\n      Write-PSFMessage -Level Warning -Message \"Choco warning: $errLine\" -Tag 'Trace', 'Get-ChocolateyPackagesNeedingUpdate'\n    }\n\n    $exitCode = $process.ExitCode\n    return $exitCode\n  }\n...existing code...\n`\n\n**This approach:**\n- Handles each line as soon as it is produced.\n- Avoids runspace errors.\n- Does not wait for process exit before processing output.\n\nLet me know if you want a more advanced solution using runspaces or PowerShell jobs!",
