              "response": "You can simply take the `.Keys` collection and cast or wrap it into a PowerShell array. For example:\n\n````powershell\n# if $configRootKeys is a [hashtable] or Dictionary<>\n# this will give you a [string[]] of key names\n[string[]]$allKeys = $configRootKeys.Keys\n\n# or, to be explicit and force string conversion:\n[string[]]$allKeys = $configRootKeys.Keys | ForEach-Object { $_.ToString() }\n\n# verify\n$allKeys.GetType().Name # should report “Object[]”\n$allKeys | % { $_.GetType().Name }  # should report “String”\n````",
