          "toolCallRounds": [
            {
              "response": "In this chat you’re only giving the assistant access to the files you explicitly “attach” or add to its working set. Those files are the only ones it can see and reason about.\n\n• Working set  \n  – A “working set” is the list of files you’ve explicitly opened or attached in this conversation.  \n  – Only files in that set are available to the assistant for reference, linking, or edits.  \n  – You can add a file to the working set by opening it in your editor and pasting it here (or by using whatever UI your Copilot‐Chat integration provides for “adding to working set”).  \n\n• #codebase  \n  – If you prefix your question with`#codebase`, you tell the assistant, “Please scan and index my entire workspace, not just the files I’ve attached.”  \n  – That triggers an automatic discovery of all files under your repo root so the assistant can answer questions about any file.  \n\nUse the working set when you only need to focus on a few files; use `#codebase`when you need the assistant to know about everything in your project.",
