      "response": [
        {
          "value": "When you prefix your prompt with`#codebase`, Copilot-Chat will scan every folder in your *workspace*, not just the one Git repo you happen to be editing. In VS Code terms:\n\n• A *workspace* can contain multiple folders (multi-root).  \n• `#codebase`tells the assistant to index *all* those folders.  \n• It does **not** stop at the root of a single Git repository—if your workspace has 3 repos open, it’ll see all 3.\n\nIf you only want it to know about one particular repo/folder, you need to either:\n\n- Attach or open just that folder’s files in the chat (“working set”), or  \n- Narrow the scope manually (e.g. by only pasting in the files you care about).",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
