      "response": [
        {
          "value": "Here’s a quick PowerShell sample showing different ways to use ForEach-Object:\n\n````powershell\n# 1) Simple per-item processing\n1..5 | ForEach-Object {\n    Write-PSFMessage -Level Info -Message \"Number: $_\" -Tag 'Sample','Trace'\n}\n\n# 2) With Begin/Process/End blocks\nGet-Process |\n  ForEach-Object -Begin { \n      Write-PSFMessage -Level Verbose -Message 'Starting process enumeration' -Tag 'Sample','Trace'\n  } -Process {\n      Write-PSFMessage -Level Debug -Message \"Process: $($_.ProcessName) (ID: $($_.Id))\" -Tag 'Sample','Trace'\n  } -End {\n      Write-PSFMessage -Level Verbose -Message 'Finished process enumeration' -Tag 'Sample','Trace'\n  }\n\n# 3) Using the alias (%) and pipeline variable\n'apple','banana','cherry' |\n  % { Write-PSFMessage -Level Info -Message \"Fruit: $_\" -Tag 'Sample','Trace' }\n```# 1) Simple per-item processing\n1..5 | ForEach-Object {\n    Write-PSFMessage -Level Info -Message \"Number: $_\" -Tag 'Sample','Trace'\n}\n\n# 2) With Begin/Process/End blocks\nGet-Process |\n  ForEach-Object -Begin { \n      Write-PSFMessage -Level Verbose -Message 'Starting process enumeration' -Tag 'Sample','Trace'\n  } -Process {\n      Write-PSFMessage -Level Debug -Message \"Process: $($_.ProcessName) (ID: $($_.Id))\" -Tag 'Sample','Trace'\n  } -End {\n      Write-PSFMessage -Level Verbose -Message 'Finished process enumeration' -Tag 'Sample','Trace'\n  }\n\n# 3) Using the alias (%) and pipeline variable\n'apple','banana','cherry' |\n  % { Write-PSFMessage -Level Info -Message \"Fruit: $_\" -Tag 'Sample','Trace' }\n",
