      "response": [
        {
          "value": "Here’s the basic `foreach`syntax in PowerShell for iterating over a collection of`[Guid]` objects:\n\n````powershell\n# Example collection of GUIDs\n$guids = @(\n  [Guid]::NewGuid(),\n  [Guid]::NewGuid(),\n  [Guid]::NewGuid()\n)\n\n# Loop over each GUID\nforeach ($guid in $guids) {\n    Write-PSFMessage -Level Verbose `\n -Message \"Processing GUID: $guid\" `\n                    -Tag 'Validate-WakeTimersEnabled','Trace'\n}\n````\n\nIf you already have an array of string representations of GUIDs, just cast them:\n\n````powershell\n# String GUIDs\n$stringGuids = 'd3c9f18e-6f2b-4b1f-9e8d-2f4b6a7c5d3e','f1a2b3c4-d5e6-7f89-0abc-1d2e3f4a5b6c'\n\n# Cast and loop\nforeach ($guid in $stringGuids | ForEach-Object { [Guid]$_ }) {\n Write-PSFMessage -Level Verbose `\n                    -Message \"Processing GUID: $guid\" `\n -Tag 'Validate-WakeTimersEnabled','Trace'\n}\n````",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/c:/Dropbox/whertzing/GitHub/ATAP.Utilities/src/ATAP.Utilities.IAC.Ansible.Powershell/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        }
