"response": "The `.copilot/` folder is not something you or your build process created—it’s maintained by the GitHub Copilot (and Copilot Chat) extensions in VS Code to keep local, per-repo state. Here’s what you’ll typically find in it:\n\n• A cache of your Copilot Chat conversations (transcripts, prompts & replies) \n• Local settings or experiment flags (`settings.json`, `experiments.json`, etc.) \n• Session state (tokens, shortcuts, context buffers) \n• Any repository-scoped “copilot-instructions” overrides \n\nBecause it’s purely client-side metadata, you will usually want to add `.copilot/` to your `.gitignore`. If you do want to share project-specific instructions or overrides across your team, you can check in only the subset of files (e.g. a shared `copilot-instructions.md`) and leave the rest out.",
