"toolCallRounds": [
{
"response": "Repository-scoped “copilot-instructions” let you bake your project’s own ChatGPT guidance right into the repo so every teammate (and CI) gets the same defaults. Here’s how they work:\n\n• Location \n – By convention you store them in `.copilot/copilot-instructions.md` (or `github/copilot-instructions.md` if you prefer). \n – Copilot-Chat will load that file automatically whenever it opens your repo.\n\n• Purpose \n – Override or augment the global Copilot system prompt with your own style rules, naming conventions, tag requirements, file‐scanning directives, etc. \n – Enforce project specific guidelines (e.g. “always use Write-PSFMessage for logging”, “tag every function call with the function name”).\n\n• Format \n – Written in Markdown (optionally with a little front-matter if you need structured metadata). \n – Free-form text describing your expectations—Copilot-Chat treats it as top-priority system instructions.\n\n• Versioning \n – Because it lives in your Git repo, changes to the instructions flow through your normal code review and CI. \n – Everyone on the team sees the same behavior without extra client-side setup.",
